00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:59,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:59,932 --> 00:01:02,349
<i>We're living in time.</i>

2
00:01:08,432 --> 00:01:10,949
<i>Time shows no favor to the poor or the rich,</i>

3
00:01:10,949 --> 00:01:12,849
<i>the good or the evil,</i>

4
00:01:12,849 --> 00:01:15,183
<i>the old or the young.</i>

5
00:01:15,183 --> 00:01:17,683
<i>It flows equally for everyone.</i>

6
00:01:52,092 --> 00:01:56,149
<i>In the time I was given, I live a day
that is no different from yesterday</i>

7
00:01:56,149 --> 00:01:59,649
<i>and will be no different from tomorrow.</i>

8
00:02:01,148 --> 00:02:03,416
<i>And today,</i>

9
00:02:03,416 --> 00:02:05,464
<i>as indifferently as ever,</i>

10
00:02:05,464 --> 00:02:07,483
<i>time passes without a care.</i>

11
00:02:18,016 --> 00:02:20,083
[Seoul]

12
00:02:43,583 --> 00:02:46,449
[Episode 1, Blessed Are Those Who Endure]

13
00:02:46,449 --> 00:02:49,649
[Lotto]

14
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,460
Good morning, Mr. Gong.

15
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:06,483
Yeah, Ji Hye, good morning.

16
00:03:12,524 --> 00:03:14,016
Why are you just getting here now?

17
00:03:14,016 --> 00:03:15,956
Oh, I'm a bit late.

18
00:03:15,956 --> 00:03:17,183
Well, this company sure has gotten lax.

19
00:03:17,183 --> 00:03:19,988
Good morning! Hello.

20
00:03:19,988 --> 00:03:21,616
Hi, Gong!

21
00:03:22,476 --> 00:03:24,040
Mr. Gong, good morning.

22
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:25,344
Yeah, Gi Tae, good morning.

23
00:03:25,344 --> 00:03:27,072
Yes.

24
00:03:27,072 --> 00:03:28,072
When did you get in?

25
00:03:28,072 --> 00:03:30,116
Five minutes ago.

26
00:03:40,764 --> 00:03:42,416
Oh, you're here?

27
00:03:44,424 --> 00:03:45,576
Well, how's your stomach?

28
00:03:45,576 --> 00:03:46,683
I'm perfectly fine.

29
00:03:46,683 --> 00:03:48,488
Wow!

30
00:03:48,488 --> 00:03:50,683
- You're here, Mr. Jung.
- Yeah.

31
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:53,620
Good morning, Assistant Manager Yang.

32
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:54,776
- Hey.
- Good morning.

33
00:03:54,776 --> 00:03:56,504
Yeah.

34
00:03:56,504 --> 00:03:59,283
- You're here, Assistant Manager Yang.
- Yes, you too.

35
00:04:06,252 --> 00:04:07,648
Oh, Joo Hee, Joo Hee!

36
00:04:07,648 --> 00:04:09,280
Oh, good morning.

37
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:11,656
What happened to the outlet manager
who was causing trouble?

38
00:04:11,656 --> 00:04:12,664
How did you know?

39
00:04:12,664 --> 00:04:14,184
I know everything.

40
00:04:14,184 --> 00:04:16,428
Go ahead and run, Joo Hee. You won't get far.

41
00:04:16,428 --> 00:04:18,308
Alright, let's start the meeting.

42
00:04:18,308 --> 00:04:20,016
- Okay.
- Yes.

43
00:04:28,868 --> 00:04:30,583
Well, Assistant Manager Yang, the meeting...

44
00:04:30,583 --> 00:04:31,960
- Want some coffee?
- Pardon?

45
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:34,652
No, I think we should
go to the meeting first.

46
00:04:34,652 --> 00:04:38,000
Come on, we've got to have some coffee
to get through the day.

47
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,972
- Fine. I'll go.
- Okay.

48
00:04:39,972 --> 00:04:41,616
I said I'm going.

49
00:04:53,492 --> 00:04:55,167
Let's get this over with and get to work.

50
00:04:55,167 --> 00:04:56,172
- Okay.
- Yes.

51
00:04:56,172 --> 00:04:58,572
What happened with the discrepancy
between last week's warehouse shipments

52
00:04:58,572 --> 00:04:59,720
and the department store deliveries?

53
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:02,996
Apparently, one box from the department store
warehouse had been left out.

54
00:05:02,996 --> 00:05:06,076
The quantities all match now.

55
00:05:06,076 --> 00:05:07,749
They won't actually match.

56
00:05:07,749 --> 00:05:09,349
When inventory still doesn't match,

57
00:05:09,349 --> 00:05:11,788
some stores borrow stock
from elsewhere as a quick fix.

58
00:05:11,788 --> 00:05:13,596
Make a surprise visit and check.

59
00:05:13,596 --> 00:05:14,650
Yes, understood.

60
00:05:14,650 --> 00:05:17,156
Let's just let it go this time.

61
00:05:17,156 --> 00:05:19,612
Well, it's obvious they borrowed the stock
from another store.

62
00:05:19,612 --> 00:05:22,228
Digging it up will only create bad blood.

63
00:05:22,228 --> 00:05:24,183
I think it'd be better to wait

64
00:05:24,183 --> 00:05:27,249
until sales stabilize
and check everything at once.

65
00:05:28,868 --> 00:05:31,072
Okay, let's do that.

66
00:05:31,072 --> 00:05:33,240
Then I'll make the changes accordingly.

67
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:38,383
Can we finish compiling each brand's
SS lineup by the end of this week?

68
00:05:41,444 --> 00:05:44,948
- Assistant Manager Yang.
- I'll let you know once I have it sorted out.

69
00:05:44,948 --> 00:05:47,716
We need the list by the end of this week,
so we can review it internally

70
00:05:47,716 --> 00:05:50,148
and place the orders by next week.

71
00:05:50,148 --> 00:05:53,583
It's not something I have full control over.

72
00:05:54,916 --> 00:05:57,816
Still, please check and let me know.

73
00:05:58,588 --> 00:06:00,183
Okay.

74
00:06:06,608 --> 00:06:08,140
- Ji Hye.
- Yes.

75
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:12,449
Please share the draft designs for the brands
undergoing CI changes, collect feedback,

76
00:06:12,449 --> 00:06:14,336
and create an evaluation sheet for reporting.

77
00:06:14,336 --> 00:06:15,688
Can you have it done by the end of today?

78
00:06:15,688 --> 00:06:16,912
Yes, I can.

79
00:06:16,912 --> 00:06:18,860
Let me know if it's too much.
I'm offering to help.

80
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:21,249
No, I can do it.

81
00:06:22,544 --> 00:06:24,049
And I've heard that employees

82
00:06:24,049 --> 00:06:27,228
have been using work hours too freely lately.

83
00:06:27,228 --> 00:06:28,483
Given the nature of our work,

84
00:06:28,483 --> 00:06:30,776
we can't strictly stick to
a nine-to-six schedule.

85
00:06:30,776 --> 00:06:33,674
But I'd still like everyone to follow
the company's guidelines as much as possible.

86
00:06:33,674 --> 00:06:34,678
Everyone understands, right?

87
00:06:34,678 --> 00:06:36,383
Yes.

88
00:06:42,053 --> 00:06:44,683
- Alright, back to work.
- Okay.

89
00:06:45,364 --> 00:06:46,983
Oh, dear.

90
00:06:47,952 --> 00:06:50,528
You've really got your hands full.

91
00:06:50,528 --> 00:06:53,483
I get that juniors need to be trained.

92
00:06:53,483 --> 00:06:56,212
But when an assistant manager acts like that,
there's really no hope.

93
00:06:56,212 --> 00:06:58,392
Assistant Manager Yang
must have it rough too.

94
00:06:58,392 --> 00:07:00,848
It can't be easy
working under a younger junior.

95
00:07:00,848 --> 00:07:03,836
Yeah, neither of you has it easy.

96
00:07:03,836 --> 00:07:05,052
But what is this meeting about?

97
00:07:05,052 --> 00:07:06,492
I have no idea.

98
00:07:06,492 --> 00:07:09,380
I don't know what they're up to.

99
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:10,928
Darn it.

100
00:07:10,928 --> 00:07:12,116
Oh, where are you going?

101
00:07:12,116 --> 00:07:13,372
Let's work our legs.

102
00:07:13,372 --> 00:07:14,408
What are you talking about?

103
00:07:14,408 --> 00:07:15,516
Let's take the stairs.

104
00:07:15,516 --> 00:07:17,576
[F Floor Meeting Room Reservation Status]

105
00:07:17,576 --> 00:07:19,183
Oh, dear.

106
00:07:20,220 --> 00:07:21,844
Hello.

107
00:07:21,844 --> 00:07:23,016
Hello.

108
00:07:23,016 --> 00:07:25,712
- Yes.
- Good morning.

109
00:07:25,712 --> 00:07:27,520
- Mr. Jung.
- Yes?

110
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:30,528
Am I a zombie, or are you a rat?

111
00:07:30,528 --> 00:07:31,800
What do you mean?

112
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:35,504
Well, why would you take the stairs
when there's a perfectly good elevator?

113
00:07:35,504 --> 00:07:37,440
Oh, you saw that.

114
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:39,940
I just had something to
discuss with Mr. Gong.

115
00:07:39,940 --> 00:07:44,084
I wondered if you were giving me attitude
because I objected to a few things.

116
00:07:44,084 --> 00:07:45,868
You objected to a few things?

117
00:07:45,868 --> 00:07:47,647
I don't remember that.

118
00:07:47,647 --> 00:07:49,349
Did he?

119
00:07:51,404 --> 00:07:53,940
- You're here.
- Hello.

120
00:07:53,940 --> 00:07:56,116
- Everyone's here.
- Yes.

121
00:07:56,788 --> 00:07:58,549
- Sit down.
- Okay.

122
00:08:03,968 --> 00:08:05,280
Okay.

123
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:08,352
Has everyone been given
the instructions about working hours?

124
00:08:08,352 --> 00:08:09,516
Yes.

125
00:08:09,516 --> 00:08:12,572
Someone's definitely going to get caught.
Just don't be the first one.

126
00:08:12,572 --> 00:08:14,268
I can't cover for you on that.

127
00:08:14,268 --> 00:08:15,436
Okay.

128
00:08:15,436 --> 00:08:17,856
Alright, let's start the meeting.

129
00:08:17,856 --> 00:08:19,316
Today's agenda is simple.

130
00:08:19,316 --> 00:08:20,664
[Weekly Meeting Report]

131
00:08:20,664 --> 00:08:22,416
Laknes.

132
00:08:25,704 --> 00:08:27,616
What does everyone think about this?

133
00:08:31,512 --> 00:08:33,332
Shall we go around the table?

134
00:08:33,332 --> 00:08:36,083
Or should we just rock-paper-scissors?

135
00:08:38,384 --> 00:08:41,416
Well, the design is one thing,

136
00:08:41,416 --> 00:08:43,683
but the price is way too high-end.

137
00:08:43,683 --> 00:08:46,644
The brand isn't well known,
and the collection is limited.

138
00:08:46,644 --> 00:08:48,712
And it's not like
it has a lot of patterns or prints.

139
00:08:48,712 --> 00:08:52,244
It is a difficult brand to work with.

140
00:08:52,244 --> 00:08:53,828
Anything else?

141
00:08:53,828 --> 00:08:57,180
I heard they only recently
pulled out of the Korean market.

142
00:08:57,180 --> 00:09:01,100
Maybe things would be different
if the designs or prices had changed.

143
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:04,883
But if they come back exactly the same,
won't we get the same result?

144
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:08,984
The designs were a bit challenging at first.

145
00:09:08,984 --> 00:09:10,560
But times have changed.

146
00:09:10,560 --> 00:09:12,300
It's not like they left because they failed.

147
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:14,728
I think they were once
among the top ten luxury brands.

148
00:09:14,728 --> 00:09:17,872
They ranked ninth
in women's luxury, didn't they?

149
00:09:17,872 --> 00:09:19,716
Yes, but only once.

150
00:09:19,716 --> 00:09:23,700
I understand everyone's concerns.
But we have to do this.

151
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:25,424
It's the department head's order.

152
00:09:25,424 --> 00:09:27,883
Don't take it. Hold your ground.

153
00:09:29,228 --> 00:09:32,452
Since Laknes has an avant-garde design,

154
00:09:32,452 --> 00:09:34,620
how about letting Mr. Gong handle it?

155
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:36,852
I mean, you're the youngest
and have the best taste among us.

156
00:09:36,852 --> 00:09:38,449
Don't you think?

157
00:09:40,856 --> 00:09:45,728
As you know, our team
doesn't have much capacity right now.

158
00:09:45,728 --> 00:09:49,549
We have the fewest people,
but we're handling the most brands.

159
00:09:49,549 --> 00:09:51,849
What do you say, team leaders?

160
00:09:54,380 --> 00:09:57,992
Honestly, every team
is short-staffed right now.

161
00:09:57,992 --> 00:10:02,220
If we're matching brand to fit,
Mr. Gong's team seems the best choice.

162
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:04,183
Yeah, that's probably right.

163
00:10:05,248 --> 00:10:08,868
What the team leaders said is fair.

164
00:10:08,868 --> 00:10:12,100
But I do feel like we're always
dumping work on him

165
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:14,220
just because he's the youngest team leader.

166
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:16,156
Then let Team 4 take it.

167
00:10:16,156 --> 00:10:18,949
Well, that's not what I meant.

168
00:10:18,949 --> 00:10:21,248
- Mr. Gong?
- Yes.

169
00:10:21,248 --> 00:10:23,083
How about your team takes Laknes

170
00:10:23,083 --> 00:10:28,164
and moves a few
of your current brands to another team?

171
00:10:28,164 --> 00:10:29,916
That should be doable, right?

172
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,848
Yes,

173
00:10:32,848 --> 00:10:34,604
that works.

174
00:10:34,604 --> 00:10:36,848
Okay.

175
00:10:36,848 --> 00:10:39,732
Idiot. I told you not to take it.

176
00:10:39,732 --> 00:10:41,883
What an idiot, seriously.

177
00:10:47,756 --> 00:10:50,024
I told you not to take it. Why did you?

178
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,849
- It's fine.
- Huh?

179
00:10:51,849 --> 00:10:53,946
If that's not what you meant
when you said that to him earlier,

180
00:10:53,946 --> 00:10:54,949
then what did you mean?

181
00:10:54,949 --> 00:10:58,444
Everyone was pushing it onto you,
so I was just trying to defend you...

182
00:10:58,444 --> 00:11:01,292
Mr. Gong, hold on.

183
00:11:01,292 --> 00:11:06,783
Before you decide which brands
to hand over, can you run it by me first?

184
00:11:10,236 --> 00:11:11,544
Yes, understood.

185
00:11:11,544 --> 00:11:12,640
Let's grab a drink sometime.

186
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:14,216
Okay.

187
00:11:20,696 --> 00:11:22,249
Mr. Kim.

188
00:11:23,928 --> 00:11:25,180
What is this?

189
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:27,096
It's a return. But give it to your wife.

190
00:11:27,096 --> 00:11:30,188
Oh, a scarf?

191
00:11:30,188 --> 00:11:31,608
Would Laknes work?

192
00:11:31,608 --> 00:11:32,646
Do you think it would?

193
00:11:32,646 --> 00:11:36,744
It's the same failed brand
coming back with nothing changed.

194
00:11:36,744 --> 00:11:38,503
Isn't it a bit low to take a brand from him

195
00:11:38,503 --> 00:11:40,449
while giving him one that's bound to fail?

196
00:11:40,449 --> 00:11:44,424
The deputy director is handing it to me.
What else can I do but say thanks?

197
00:11:44,424 --> 00:11:47,349
Mr. Kim, you sure are ambitious.

198
00:11:47,349 --> 00:11:51,112
So while we're at it,
why don't you give me one too?

199
00:11:51,112 --> 00:11:52,960
Pardon?

200
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,249
You want one of mine too?

201
00:11:54,249 --> 00:11:58,164
Even if the deputy director backs me,
the department head is still neutral.

202
00:11:58,164 --> 00:12:00,104
That's what worries me.

203
00:12:00,104 --> 00:12:02,520
If Team Leader Son gets
something from Team Leader Jung,

204
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:05,049
we're gonna have a real problem.

205
00:12:05,049 --> 00:12:06,280
Let's play the long game. Okay?

206
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:09,928
Just give me one decent brand, got it?

207
00:12:09,928 --> 00:12:11,583
I'll put it to good use.

208
00:12:13,496 --> 00:12:16,372
Everyone's on edge.

209
00:12:16,372 --> 00:12:19,576
They have to take Laknes
because it's the department head's order,

210
00:12:19,576 --> 00:12:21,872
but you're the only team leader
who'll do it without complaining.

211
00:12:21,872 --> 00:12:24,117
They want to promote Mr. Kim
to deputy director,

212
00:12:24,117 --> 00:12:25,672
but his sales numbers aren't high enough,

213
00:12:25,672 --> 00:12:29,252
so they're giving him one of your brands
to boost his performance.

214
00:12:29,252 --> 00:12:33,772
That's why Mr. Son's freaking out
about losing the promotion.

215
00:12:33,772 --> 00:12:36,616
And I'm being treated like
someone who doesn't matter,

216
00:12:36,616 --> 00:12:40,183
no matter which brands you hand out.

217
00:12:40,183 --> 00:12:43,248
If you really want one that much,
why not just take one?

218
00:12:43,248 --> 00:12:45,900
I just feel bad for both of us. You and me.

219
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:48,164
Give me what? I'm not taking anything.

220
00:12:48,164 --> 00:12:49,564
Well, I'm fine either way.

221
00:12:49,564 --> 00:12:52,148
Since they're taking them away anyway,
I'd be happy if they grow them well.

222
00:12:52,148 --> 00:12:54,936
If you're putting it up for adoption,
you want good parents, right?

223
00:12:54,936 --> 00:12:57,896
But don't just let them take them from you.

224
00:12:57,896 --> 00:12:59,756
Push back a little.

225
00:12:59,756 --> 00:13:04,188
Say, "I can't do Laknes.
I'll keep my own sales."

226
00:13:04,188 --> 00:13:06,556
But honestly, even I think

227
00:13:06,556 --> 00:13:08,083
I'm the only one who can handle Laknes.

228
00:13:08,083 --> 00:13:09,552
You wouldn't take it, either.

229
00:13:09,552 --> 00:13:13,516
Exactly. I don't want it either,
so why are you taking it?

230
00:13:13,516 --> 00:13:16,020
And since we're on the subject,
your team is the same.

231
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:18,912
They always take on the jobs
nobody else wants and suffer for them.

232
00:13:18,912 --> 00:13:21,700
Once they've worked hard to build them up,
someone else comes along and takes them.

233
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:23,936
What's the point of that?

234
00:13:23,936 --> 00:13:25,949
Is this supposed to make me feel better?

235
00:13:25,949 --> 00:13:29,256
I'm saying it because
I feel bad for you. I really do.

236
00:13:29,256 --> 00:13:33,016
I mean, I'm basically
the unwanted child here,

237
00:13:33,016 --> 00:13:35,992
but you're clearly
in Deputy Director Jang's line.

238
00:13:35,992 --> 00:13:37,949
Why is Deputy Director Jang acting like this?

239
00:13:37,949 --> 00:13:40,932
He raised you, so he should
take responsibility for you.

240
00:13:40,932 --> 00:13:42,564
Why does it always have to be like this?

241
00:13:42,564 --> 00:13:45,128
Even you have to admit... what?

242
00:13:45,128 --> 00:13:47,416
Ugh, that rude punk.

243
00:13:47,416 --> 00:13:49,183
Hey, let's go together.

244
00:13:58,060 --> 00:14:00,416
- Gong, good work.
- Bye.

245
00:14:10,332 --> 00:14:11,976
I'm heading out.

246
00:14:11,976 --> 00:14:13,849
Yeah, go ahead.

247
00:14:15,472 --> 00:14:17,244
Wow, I'm hungry.

248
00:14:17,244 --> 00:14:18,680
Let's get some food. What should we have?

249
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:22,664
Well, then how about that BBQ place
we went to last time?

250
00:14:22,664 --> 00:14:25,104
It's way too cheap there. You're paying.

251
00:14:25,104 --> 00:14:26,988
Oh, I'm paying?

252
00:14:26,988 --> 00:14:29,516
Aren't you coming with us, Mr. Gong?

253
00:14:30,488 --> 00:14:32,064
No, I'm good.

254
00:14:32,064 --> 00:14:33,912
Okay, then I'll head home first.

255
00:14:33,912 --> 00:14:36,020
Then I'll head out too.

256
00:14:36,020 --> 00:14:38,516
Then let's go with whatever Ji Hye wants.

257
00:14:38,516 --> 00:14:40,480
- Ji Hye?
- Whatever I want?

258
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:42,584
Ji Hye is a pig, right?

259
00:14:42,584 --> 00:14:43,928
- Ji Hye's a pig?
- Yes.

260
00:14:43,928 --> 00:14:45,488
If we eat pork again,
we're gonna end up having soju and beer.

261
00:14:45,488 --> 00:14:46,620
Oh, soju and beer!

262
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:47,824
- Nice.
- Oh.

263
00:14:47,824 --> 00:14:48,868
Going hard again tonight?

264
00:14:48,868 --> 00:14:51,483
Sure. I'm down for anything.

265
00:14:57,568 --> 00:14:59,983
[Train approaching
Stand by]

266
00:14:59,983 --> 00:15:02,449
[Stop]

267
00:15:08,428 --> 00:15:10,340
What did the hospital say?

268
00:15:10,340 --> 00:15:11,504
About your father?

269
00:15:11,504 --> 00:15:14,400
Oh, he got the tests done,

270
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:15,908
but the results aren't out yet.

271
00:15:15,908 --> 00:15:17,784
But they said there's no need
to worry too much.

272
00:15:17,784 --> 00:15:19,308
Still, keep an eye on him.

273
00:15:19,308 --> 00:15:20,983
Older people aren't like us.

274
00:15:20,983 --> 00:15:22,456
Okay, I will.

275
00:15:22,456 --> 00:15:23,792
Let me know when the results are out.

276
00:15:23,792 --> 00:15:26,816
If it comes to it,
I can refer you to another hospital.

277
00:15:26,816 --> 00:15:30,516
Really? Oh, thank you.

278
00:15:31,576 --> 00:15:33,104
Ji Hye, are you busy?

279
00:15:33,104 --> 00:15:34,260
Oh, no.

280
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:36,136
Then how about you handle the tongs?

281
00:15:36,136 --> 00:15:37,828
Oh, give them to me.

282
00:15:37,828 --> 00:15:40,080
No, I can do this.

283
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:43,200
Why? Because Ji Hye's a woman?

284
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:45,249
Or because she's a contract worker?

285
00:15:45,249 --> 00:15:47,756
Oh, no, it's not that.

286
00:15:47,756 --> 00:15:50,683
Whether man or woman,
contract worker or permanent employee,

287
00:15:50,683 --> 00:15:52,476
Ji Hye's one of us.

288
00:15:52,476 --> 00:15:54,304
Aren't you the youngest?

289
00:15:54,304 --> 00:15:58,412
Yes, I am.
I should've grilled it sooner, sorry.

290
00:15:58,412 --> 00:16:01,012
I don't know what Mr. Gong thinks,

291
00:16:01,012 --> 00:16:04,848
but I'm not letting her go
once her contract ends.

292
00:16:04,848 --> 00:16:06,732
- Pardon?
- Just wait.

293
00:16:06,732 --> 00:16:08,544
I'm not sucking up to all these
team leaders, directors,

294
00:16:08,544 --> 00:16:10,196
and department heads for nothing.

295
00:16:10,196 --> 00:16:12,032
I'm trying to secure a favor.

296
00:16:12,032 --> 00:16:15,744
I'd do anything for it. For your sake.

297
00:16:15,744 --> 00:16:18,568
Yes. Thank you, Assistant Manager Yang.

298
00:16:18,568 --> 00:16:20,648
If you're grateful, grill the meat.
It's burning already.

299
00:16:20,648 --> 00:16:22,080
Oh, I'm sorry.

300
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:23,949
Have a drink, have a drink.

301
00:17:14,912 --> 00:17:18,683
Mr. Gong, you have
such good posture, don't you?

302
00:17:21,148 --> 00:17:22,629
After seven years at the company,

303
00:17:22,629 --> 00:17:26,368
isn't it only natural
to have tech neck and scoliosis?

304
00:17:26,368 --> 00:17:29,884
Dry eyes and fatty liver should be enough.

305
00:17:29,884 --> 00:17:31,304
Leaving late?

306
00:17:31,304 --> 00:17:33,949
This is early for me.

307
00:17:35,184 --> 00:17:37,176
You look happy.

308
00:17:37,176 --> 00:17:39,516
I'm pretending to be.

309
00:17:41,449 --> 00:17:42,649
Heading home?

310
00:17:42,649 --> 00:17:43,888
I have plans.

311
00:17:43,888 --> 00:17:45,744
Let's grab a drink.

312
00:17:45,744 --> 00:17:47,116
I told you I have plans.

313
00:17:47,116 --> 00:17:49,980
Let's get some puffer fish soup
and split the bill.

314
00:17:49,980 --> 00:17:52,249
I have plans.

315
00:17:52,904 --> 00:17:55,349
You don't have plans.

316
00:17:57,348 --> 00:17:59,016
Come on.

317
00:18:00,516 --> 00:18:02,008
[Cheongjin Bok]

318
00:18:02,008 --> 00:18:04,636
Ma'am, one more bottle here!

319
00:18:04,636 --> 00:18:06,983
Thank you.

320
00:18:13,624 --> 00:18:17,372
Why are you always by yourself?

321
00:18:17,372 --> 00:18:21,149
The other team leaders
are always taking their teams out.

322
00:18:22,032 --> 00:18:24,668
Your team leader
doesn't hang out with you, either.

323
00:18:24,668 --> 00:18:27,160
Isn't it probably for the same reason
as your team leader?

324
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:30,776
Exactly. I'm just a lowly team member.

325
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:33,760
I'm asking because you're the team leader.

326
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:35,783
The legal team leader is equivalent
to a managing director,

327
00:18:35,783 --> 00:18:37,416
so technically, you're above me.

328
00:18:37,416 --> 00:18:39,696
Ugh, seriously.

329
00:18:39,696 --> 00:18:41,578
One of our peers was so happy to
become a team leader

330
00:18:41,578 --> 00:18:43,568
that he even treated the team to beef.

331
00:18:43,568 --> 00:18:47,156
But now you can't even join your team.
You just wander around alone.

332
00:18:47,156 --> 00:18:50,100
And what's that thing? Laknes.

333
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:53,112
And there you are,
playing the sucker in a rigged game.

334
00:18:53,112 --> 00:18:55,480
What did you even become a team leader for?

335
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:59,616
The company has a bigger plan for Laknes.

336
00:18:59,616 --> 00:19:03,608
I'm just one piece of the background.

337
00:19:03,608 --> 00:19:06,460
Fine, let's say
that's the company's big picture.

338
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:10,112
Then why is Assistant Manager Yang
drawing the picture for your team?

339
00:19:10,112 --> 00:19:12,900
I hear Assistant Manager Yang
is always taking the team around.

340
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:17,264
Isn't he making you do the dirty work
while he plays the team leader?

341
00:19:17,264 --> 00:19:21,749
Even if he's senior to you,
isn't that crossing a line?

342
00:19:24,780 --> 00:19:26,483
Assistant Manager Yang...

343
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:30,449
Darn it, he's annoying.

344
00:19:30,449 --> 00:19:32,128
Right.

345
00:19:32,128 --> 00:19:33,596
But on the other hand,

346
00:19:33,596 --> 00:19:37,984
even if he gets on my nerves
playing the team leader,

347
00:19:37,984 --> 00:19:40,216
maybe it's fine

348
00:19:40,216 --> 00:19:43,960
as long as the numbers are good
and the work gets done.

349
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:46,508
We're here to work, after all.

350
00:19:46,508 --> 00:19:49,712
So everything's okay
as long as the work gets done?

351
00:19:49,712 --> 00:19:51,440
But you're the one who's suffering.

352
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:54,316
If I suffer and the work
gets done, then I'm...

353
00:19:54,972 --> 00:19:56,764
I'm fine with it.

354
00:19:56,764 --> 00:19:59,724
Wow. Is this a company or a monastery?

355
00:19:59,724 --> 00:20:02,416
You're gonna attain enlightenment
working here.

356
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:14,416
I'm off. Good work.

357
00:20:14,416 --> 00:20:17,060
What do you mean, "good work"? I'm done.

358
00:20:17,060 --> 00:20:20,283
Always "good work."

359
00:20:20,928 --> 00:20:23,668
You've still got a whole day left?

360
00:20:23,668 --> 00:20:26,316
Jeez, Gong Eun Tae.

361
00:20:35,452 --> 00:20:36,949
Good work!

362
00:21:16,164 --> 00:21:18,983
<i>What kind of life am I living?</i>

363
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:38,124
Sir, are you okay?

364
00:21:38,124 --> 00:21:39,949
- Yeah.
- Let me help you.

365
00:21:42,349 --> 00:21:47,183
<i>I was born into a family
that was neither rich nor poor.</i>

366
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:50,708
<i>If I worked hard, I could move up,</i>

367
00:21:50,708 --> 00:21:53,849
<i>but I could also fall down just as easily.</i>

368
00:21:53,849 --> 00:21:55,092
[Gong Eun Tae]

369
00:21:55,092 --> 00:21:57,216
<i>So I always worked hard.</i>

370
00:22:01,048 --> 00:22:04,116
<i>I wanted to get into a better university</i>

371
00:22:05,383 --> 00:22:08,449
<i>and land a better job.</i>

372
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:19,983
<i>Regardless of the outcome,
working hard at something made me feel secure.</i>

373
00:22:20,772 --> 00:22:25,416
<i>It made me feel like
I was living my life the right way.</i>

374
00:22:36,284 --> 00:22:40,132
<i>Hongsung International
was the job I got that way.</i>

375
00:22:40,132 --> 00:22:43,049
<i>It ranks second in its field by revenue.</i>

376
00:22:43,049 --> 00:22:45,749
<i>It ranks third
in the number of brands it operates,</i>

377
00:22:45,749 --> 00:22:47,572
<i>with 800 billion won in revenue.</i>

378
00:22:47,572 --> 00:22:51,096
<i>It is a large company
with nearly 900 employees.</i>

379
00:22:51,096 --> 00:22:53,696
[Hongsung International]
<i>My parents didn't know the company name,</i>

380
00:22:53,696 --> 00:22:57,549
<i>but they were proud that
I worked for a major corporation.</i>

381
00:22:57,549 --> 00:23:02,883
<i>And I was grateful to be able to
make a living on my own.</i>

382
00:23:03,640 --> 00:23:07,183
[Team Leader Gong Eun Tae]
<i>Nothing's changed after becoming an employee.</i>

383
00:23:07,183 --> 00:23:10,368
<i>I still live within set boundaries,</i>

384
00:23:10,368 --> 00:23:13,128
<i>following the prescribed schedule.</i>

385
00:23:13,128 --> 00:23:15,716
<i>And, as always, I give it my all.</i>

386
00:23:16,980 --> 00:23:21,633
<i>After three years of being
the first to arrive and the last to leave,</i>

387
00:23:21,633 --> 00:23:24,749
<i>I was promoted to assistant manager.</i>

388
00:23:26,276 --> 00:23:29,183
<i>Three more years of the same,
and I became a team leader.</i>

389
00:23:29,183 --> 00:23:33,649
[Hongsung International]

390
00:23:48,616 --> 00:23:53,983
[Elltz Tower]

391
00:23:56,884 --> 00:24:01,749
<i>And in return, I got the deposit back
on my studio apartment,</i>

392
00:24:02,736 --> 00:24:05,700
<i>a little fatty liver, and dry eyes.</i>

393
00:24:05,700 --> 00:24:08,383
<i>And a mild case of a slipped disc.</i>

394
00:24:12,583 --> 00:24:14,816
<i>Does everyone live like this?</i>

395
00:24:16,784 --> 00:24:20,949
<i>Would life get a little better
if I worked a little harder?</i>

396
00:24:24,392 --> 00:24:27,549
<i>What was I working so hard for?</i>

397
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:39,316
<i>And since when did I stop living that way?</i>

398
00:24:46,612 --> 00:24:48,116
Yes?

399
00:24:48,116 --> 00:24:49,783
Oh, hello.

400
00:24:49,783 --> 00:24:51,149
Here are the clothes you left with us.

401
00:24:51,149 --> 00:24:53,260
Oh, yes. Thank you.

402
00:24:53,260 --> 00:24:54,883
Oh, and sir.

403
00:24:54,883 --> 00:24:58,084
We seem to have lost one of your shirts.

404
00:24:58,084 --> 00:24:59,916
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

405
00:25:01,356 --> 00:25:03,564
Which shirt was it?

406
00:25:03,564 --> 00:25:07,592
My wife just said the number of clothes
didn't match the owner's record,

407
00:25:07,592 --> 00:25:09,860
so I don't know which shirt it was.

408
00:25:09,860 --> 00:25:13,256
Well, then this...

409
00:25:13,256 --> 00:25:14,916
All right, then.

410
00:25:21,076 --> 00:25:25,483
<i>And since when did I stop getting angry?</i>

411
00:25:29,716 --> 00:25:34,416
[Hankyung Bank]

412
00:25:41,064 --> 00:25:43,083
Oh? Assistant Manager Yang!

413
00:25:43,083 --> 00:25:44,524
Oh, Joo Hee, Joo Hee!

414
00:25:44,524 --> 00:25:45,749
Good morning.

415
00:25:45,749 --> 00:25:48,032
Good morning.

416
00:25:48,032 --> 00:25:51,049
Why do you look so exhausted coming to work?

417
00:25:51,049 --> 00:25:53,224
Anyone who's energetic
on the way to work is the weird one.

418
00:25:53,224 --> 00:25:54,683
Watch out for those people.

419
00:25:54,683 --> 00:25:58,683
Oh, is this about reorganizing the brands?

420
00:25:59,716 --> 00:26:03,104
Reorganizing the brands?
What are you talking about?

421
00:26:03,104 --> 00:26:05,316
Didn't you know?

422
00:26:08,936 --> 00:26:10,036
Good morning.

423
00:26:10,036 --> 00:26:11,616
Yes.

424
00:26:12,896 --> 00:26:14,749
- Good morning.
- Yes.

425
00:26:16,180 --> 00:26:18,437
- Good morning, Assistant Manager Yang.
- Good morning.

426
00:26:18,437 --> 00:26:19,449
You're here.

427
00:26:19,449 --> 00:26:21,549
- Assistant Manager Yang...
- A word please.

428
00:26:42,280 --> 00:26:45,240
Well, what's this about?

429
00:26:45,240 --> 00:26:49,749
What does that mean,
handing some brands over to another team?

430
00:26:53,083 --> 00:26:54,544
That's how it worked out.

431
00:26:54,544 --> 00:26:56,216
So why?

432
00:26:58,092 --> 00:27:00,183
We've agreed to take on Laknes.

433
00:27:00,183 --> 00:27:04,483
Since it's being relaunched,
it'll need a lot of work.

434
00:27:04,483 --> 00:27:10,676
So... we've decided to hand
some of our existing brands

435
00:27:10,676 --> 00:27:13,149
over to other teams.

436
00:27:14,456 --> 00:27:17,049
Isn't this a bit too much?

437
00:27:18,104 --> 00:27:22,928
Has any of the brands
we've handled ever been normal?

438
00:27:22,928 --> 00:27:24,549
Ainard?

439
00:27:25,340 --> 00:27:29,748
Fine, maybe we can say we took Ainard
because Team 3 couldn't handle the sales.

440
00:27:29,748 --> 00:27:31,784
But what about the rest?

441
00:27:31,784 --> 00:27:34,724
Wasn't every single one of those brands
on the verge of being dropped?

442
00:27:34,724 --> 00:27:37,332
We took them all, turned them around,

443
00:27:37,332 --> 00:27:38,596
and then they got taken away from us again.

444
00:27:38,596 --> 00:27:42,012
And now we're taking on a hopeless Laknes?

445
00:27:42,012 --> 00:27:45,228
No matter how powerless the team leader is,

446
00:27:45,228 --> 00:27:48,016
is it okay for the team members
to be treated like this?

447
00:27:50,744 --> 00:27:52,416
Assistant Manager Yang.

448
00:27:53,440 --> 00:27:57,512
Do you think I want to just sit back

449
00:27:57,512 --> 00:28:00,656
and let them take the brands I manage?

450
00:28:00,656 --> 00:28:02,788
Mr. Gong,

451
00:28:02,788 --> 00:28:06,992
I have one favor to ask you.

452
00:28:06,992 --> 00:28:09,532
Let us keep the brands we've been managing.

453
00:28:09,532 --> 00:28:11,403
You've gotta at least
do this much for us to decide

454
00:28:11,403 --> 00:28:14,424
whether to trust you and follow you, right?

455
00:28:14,424 --> 00:28:16,949
This isn't a difficult thing to ask.

456
00:28:18,216 --> 00:28:22,024
Just let us keep doing our jobs.

457
00:28:22,024 --> 00:28:23,616
Okay?

458
00:28:46,728 --> 00:28:48,349
Oh, boy.

459
00:29:03,932 --> 00:29:05,916
Did Assistant Manager Yang confront you?

460
00:29:07,332 --> 00:29:10,749
Darn, Assistant Manager Yang, seriously...

461
00:29:13,976 --> 00:29:16,252
He's right about all of it.

462
00:29:16,252 --> 00:29:19,224
If a team leader can't earn
their team's trust, it's over.

463
00:29:19,224 --> 00:29:22,283
So Assistant Manager Yang
is pushing back against you.

464
00:29:22,283 --> 00:29:23,996
What are you going to do?

465
00:29:23,996 --> 00:29:26,416
Don't you think you need to push back too?

466
00:29:28,824 --> 00:29:32,152
Have you ever seen me get angry?

467
00:29:32,152 --> 00:29:35,248
Have I seen you angry?

468
00:29:35,248 --> 00:29:37,052
No, I haven't.

469
00:29:37,052 --> 00:29:39,884
When I'm angry, I don't get angry.

470
00:29:39,884 --> 00:29:43,716
If I lose my temper,
I'm the one who has to clean up the mess.

471
00:29:43,716 --> 00:29:47,104
Who worries about that when they're angry?

472
00:29:47,104 --> 00:29:49,383
When you're angry, you just get angry.

473
00:29:52,628 --> 00:29:55,760
So what are you going to do now?

474
00:29:55,760 --> 00:29:58,020
I have to do something.

475
00:29:58,020 --> 00:29:59,783
Like what?

476
00:30:09,476 --> 00:30:10,583
Is he inside?

477
00:30:10,583 --> 00:30:12,316
Yes.

478
00:30:23,784 --> 00:30:25,349
Come in.

479
00:30:33,280 --> 00:30:34,792
What is it?

480
00:30:34,792 --> 00:30:36,422
I have something to say.

481
00:30:36,422 --> 00:30:39,620
- Is it gonna take long?
- I don't think it'll be short.

482
00:30:39,620 --> 00:30:41,283
Sit down.

483
00:30:49,740 --> 00:30:51,283
What is it?

484
00:30:52,560 --> 00:30:56,849
I'd appreciate it if you'd reconsider
the Laknes assignment.

485
00:31:00,172 --> 00:31:03,916
You think taking Laknes
is hurting your team's morale?

486
00:31:05,068 --> 00:31:07,016
What did Yang Jun Ho say?

487
00:31:09,520 --> 00:31:11,036
Tell me.

488
00:31:11,036 --> 00:31:15,148
Of all your subordinates, Yang Jun Ho
is the only one who'd dare object, isn't?

489
00:31:15,148 --> 00:31:18,883
No. They all feel the same way.

490
00:31:34,176 --> 00:31:35,816
Hey.

491
00:31:37,080 --> 00:31:39,849
How long are you gonna
let your team push you around?

492
00:31:40,612 --> 00:31:43,508
If you really can't handle it, I'll take it.

493
00:31:43,508 --> 00:31:45,908
I can give it to another team.

494
00:31:45,908 --> 00:31:47,720
But that's not the case.

495
00:31:47,720 --> 00:31:49,279
You can handle anything,

496
00:31:49,279 --> 00:31:50,383
yet your own subordinates
are rebelling against you.

497
00:31:50,383 --> 00:31:54,892
You were even taking deep breaths
before you came in to see me, weren't you?

498
00:31:54,892 --> 00:31:58,283
Did I make you a team leader
just to dump unwanted work on you?

499
00:32:00,200 --> 00:32:03,383
No. I've never thought that.

500
00:32:05,164 --> 00:32:07,616
You little punk. Is that what you think?

501
00:32:11,484 --> 00:32:14,376
Keeping something that's already
doing well on track isn't hard.

502
00:32:14,376 --> 00:32:17,964
Anyone with a decent head
on their shoulders can do that.

503
00:32:17,964 --> 00:32:19,649
But...

504
00:32:21,028 --> 00:32:23,716
bringing something
that's dying back to life is hard.

505
00:32:24,352 --> 00:32:26,496
Not everyone can do that.

506
00:32:26,496 --> 00:32:30,192
I give you jobs like that
because I believe in you.

507
00:32:30,192 --> 00:32:32,300
It'll be hard for you, yeah.

508
00:32:32,300 --> 00:32:34,916
Your team will have complaints too.
But what can you do?

509
00:32:34,916 --> 00:32:38,383
You always get the job done,
no matter what I give you.

510
00:32:42,652 --> 00:32:44,784
Just hang in there.

511
00:32:44,784 --> 00:32:47,792
And just get it done.

512
00:32:47,792 --> 00:32:49,649
It all adds up.

513
00:32:54,412 --> 00:32:56,083
Get out.

514
00:33:22,324 --> 00:33:24,983
Oh, jeez.

515
00:33:26,520 --> 00:33:29,216
Gi Tae, let's go have a smoke.

516
00:33:29,216 --> 00:33:31,183
Oh, yes.

517
00:33:32,416 --> 00:33:34,516
Ji Hye, you should get some fresh air too.

518
00:33:34,516 --> 00:33:36,224
Oh, okay.

519
00:33:36,224 --> 00:33:38,268
Darn it.

520
00:34:16,016 --> 00:34:20,049
[Butcher Shop]

521
00:34:29,549 --> 00:34:31,283
[Unavailable in the current mode]

522
00:34:32,683 --> 00:34:34,383
[Unavailable in the current mode]

523
00:34:36,140 --> 00:34:39,032
I'm sorry, but our POS system
isn't working right now.

524
00:34:39,032 --> 00:34:41,608
Okay. What should I do, then?

525
00:34:41,608 --> 00:34:43,608
Do you have cash?

526
00:34:43,608 --> 00:34:45,216
Yes.

527
00:34:48,552 --> 00:34:51,116
- Here you go.
- I got 10,000 won.

528
00:34:58,448 --> 00:35:00,536
We don't have any change right now.

529
00:35:00,536 --> 00:35:02,216
I'll come back another time.

530
00:35:05,480 --> 00:35:07,449
Would you like a Lotto ticket?

531
00:35:08,312 --> 00:35:09,616
What?

532
00:35:09,616 --> 00:35:13,149
Beer is 5,000 won and a Lotto ticket is 5,000,
so that's exactly 10,000 won.

533
00:35:15,744 --> 00:35:17,036
Okay, then I'll take one.

534
00:35:17,036 --> 00:35:18,683
Okay.

535
00:35:23,692 --> 00:35:25,483
Would you like a quick pick?

536
00:35:26,528 --> 00:35:28,083
Alright.

537
00:35:33,896 --> 00:35:35,583
Here you go.

538
00:35:42,668 --> 00:35:45,176
Aren't you giving me a bag?

539
00:35:45,176 --> 00:35:47,549
You didn't pay the 100 won for the bag.

540
00:36:26,183 --> 00:36:29,683
[Mother]

541
00:36:33,572 --> 00:36:35,252
Yes, Mother.

542
00:36:35,252 --> 00:36:36,888
Have you eaten?

543
00:36:36,888 --> 00:36:38,640
<i>Yes, I'm eating now.</i>

544
00:36:38,640 --> 00:36:40,649
Do you have anything to eat at home?

545
00:36:40,649 --> 00:36:42,616
<i>Should I send you some side dishes?</i>

546
00:36:42,616 --> 00:36:45,252
I still have plenty of
what you sent last time, so I'm fine.

547
00:36:45,252 --> 00:36:47,310
<i>That was ages ago.</i>

548
00:36:47,310 --> 00:36:49,476
You should eat it already.

549
00:36:49,476 --> 00:36:52,760
Anyway, let me know
if you need more side dishes.

550
00:36:52,760 --> 00:36:54,488
Okay, I'll tell you if I need them.

551
00:36:54,488 --> 00:36:57,188
<i>Oh, and one more thing...</i>

552
00:36:57,188 --> 00:37:00,052
Well, it's nothing else...

553
00:37:00,052 --> 00:37:03,216
Can you send 5 million won to your brother?

554
00:37:04,388 --> 00:37:05,848
What happened this time?

555
00:37:05,848 --> 00:37:09,549
<i>Well, your brother
was working the night shift,</i>

556
00:37:09,549 --> 00:37:11,949
<i>and some drunk people got into a fight.</i>

557
00:37:11,949 --> 00:37:15,260
<i>He tried to break it up,
and one of them fell and injured his back.</i>

558
00:37:15,260 --> 00:37:18,283
Now they're demanding
he pay the medical bills, causing a big fuss.

559
00:37:18,283 --> 00:37:19,760
But where's he supposed to get the money?

560
00:37:19,760 --> 00:37:23,860
<i>After paying for the kids' tuition
and living expenses, he has nothing left.</i>

561
00:37:23,860 --> 00:37:25,044
I'll call him.

562
00:37:25,044 --> 00:37:26,868
<i>Oh, no, don't.</i>

563
00:37:26,868 --> 00:37:29,949
Eun Seok doesn't know I called you.

564
00:37:29,949 --> 00:37:31,783
He'll find out anyway.

565
00:37:31,783 --> 00:37:33,849
I'll call him.

566
00:37:41,283 --> 00:37:45,983
[Gong Eun Seok]

567
00:37:45,983 --> 00:37:49,783
[My brother]

568
00:37:58,684 --> 00:38:01,088
<i>Oh, yeah, Eun Tae?</i>

569
00:38:01,088 --> 00:38:02,816
Yeah, you need money?

570
00:38:02,816 --> 00:38:05,792
Oh gosh, Mom told you again, didn't she?

571
00:38:05,792 --> 00:38:08,116
I told her not to tell you.

572
00:38:08,116 --> 00:38:09,604
5 million enough?

573
00:38:09,604 --> 00:38:10,983
<i>Yeah, that'll do.</i>

574
00:38:10,983 --> 00:38:13,616
<i>Lend it to me for now,
and I'll pay you back soon.</i>

575
00:38:13,616 --> 00:38:15,608
When will you pay me back?

576
00:38:15,608 --> 00:38:18,364
Huh? When?

577
00:38:18,364 --> 00:38:21,156
Well, when? Let's see...

578
00:38:21,156 --> 00:38:24,183
Do you know how much
you've borrowed from me so far?

579
00:38:25,312 --> 00:38:28,452
<i>Just ask me for it. Why always "borrow"?</i>

580
00:38:28,452 --> 00:38:31,168
No, I really have to pay you back.

581
00:38:31,168 --> 00:38:32,864
<i>Eun Seok,</i>

582
00:38:32,864 --> 00:38:34,314
you think everyone who works at a company

583
00:38:34,314 --> 00:38:36,984
saves money and lives comfortably, right?

584
00:38:36,984 --> 00:38:39,028
I actually have no money.

585
00:38:39,028 --> 00:38:42,916
<i>Do you know how much it costs
just to breathe in Seoul?</i>

586
00:38:44,332 --> 00:38:46,383
<i>We're family.</i>

587
00:38:47,928 --> 00:38:50,388
<i>Even if we can't help each other,</i>

588
00:38:50,388 --> 00:38:52,749
let's not make things harder for each other.

589
00:38:54,024 --> 00:38:56,516
Okay. I'm sorry.

590
00:38:57,648 --> 00:38:59,036
I'll transfer it now.

591
00:38:59,036 --> 00:39:01,149
<i>Yeah, okay.</i>

592
00:39:05,249 --> 00:39:06,349
[Please enter your PIN]

593
00:39:06,349 --> 00:39:09,816
[5 million won transferred to Gong Eun Seok]

594
00:39:50,983 --> 00:39:53,683
[Stomach Health]

595
00:40:14,392 --> 00:40:17,188
The possibilities that we can refer to.

596
00:40:17,188 --> 00:40:20,028
Like "who", "that" or something like that.

597
00:40:20,028 --> 00:40:22,100
But can we have some help.

598
00:40:22,100 --> 00:40:23,952
With the word "a".

599
00:40:23,952 --> 00:40:27,849
When we find an "a" in the sentence...

600
00:41:20,716 --> 00:41:25,749
[Six Lotto winners to take home
KRW 1.9 billion each]

601
00:42:08,249 --> 00:42:12,916
[Congratulations!
You won 1,977,507,240 won total]

602
00:42:43,440 --> 00:42:46,296
Oh, man. I can't do this anymore.

603
00:42:46,296 --> 00:42:47,480
Are you heading home?

604
00:42:47,480 --> 00:42:51,816
Yeah. I feel like
I'll die if I stay any longer.

605
00:42:51,816 --> 00:42:53,220
Me too.

606
00:42:53,220 --> 00:42:54,508
Then why aren't you leaving?

607
00:42:54,508 --> 00:42:57,752
If I go home now, I'll die tomorrow.

608
00:42:57,752 --> 00:43:00,344
Everyone's living day by day.

609
00:43:00,344 --> 00:43:02,808
Wrap things up and go home.

610
00:43:02,808 --> 00:43:04,383
Take care.

611
00:43:16,249 --> 00:43:21,949
[This week's work list]

612
00:44:31,249 --> 00:44:35,983
[Did you get off work?]

